WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.375
Step three is DDoS protection.

2
00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:06.925
Every public I P in Azure gets
infrastructure protection at no cost.

3
00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:12.009
Learn's tier comparison says Network
Protection and I P Protection add adaptive

4
00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:16.107
tuning, attack analytics, metrics,
alerts and mitigation reports;

5
00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:20.812
Network Protection also adds the Rapid
Response team and cost protection.

6
00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:24.787
Choose Network Protection when
many public I Ps need coverage,

7
00:00:24.787 --> 00:00:28.762
and I P Protection for a few critical
ones, and record the choice.

8
00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:32.911
Both work at layers three and
four, so layer seven needs the web

9
00:00:32.911 --> 00:00:37.549
application firewall, and neither
covers a public I P on a NAT gateway.

10
00:00:37.549 --> 00:00:42.181
Create one plan, link each virtual
network, turn on diagnostic logs,

11
00:00:42.181 --> 00:00:46.812
and alert on the metric that reads
one while an attack is mitigated.

12
00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:49.087
Then hold it with policy in step nine.

13
00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:54.914
Exercise the response: Learn allows simulations
only through approved partners, only

14
00:00:54.914 --> 00:01:00.240
against your own protected I Ps, and one
partner, Red Button, is public cloud only.
